{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Cap total household benefits payments at 50% of the average wage",
        "additional_details": "Some data suggests that around 7% of UK families received \u00a325,000 or more per year from state support. Some may feel that it is preferable to stay on benefits rather than try to earn the same amount. We think this is an affront and disgrace to all taxpayers. We feel this proposal brings fairness to the issue and could help drive some to get a job, and help stop illegal and possibly legal immigration in its tracks.",
        "background": "Introduce a policy where a maximum benefit payment, to an individual or family, cannot exceed 50% of the published national average wage. We are concerned that paying more could exceed the take home pay of the average wage.",
